1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,820
 The love of God, whatever you do in an interview process,

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,880
 do not forget to ask the high performer question.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,360
 Despite my current garb, I just got back from the gym.

4
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:08,120
 I have been in a lot of interviews

5
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:09,120
 in a lot of corporate settings,

6
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:10,840
 and the high performer question always kills.

7
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:12,240
 It's very simple, it sounds like this.

8
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,920
 You're gonna interview, this is you asking the interviewer.

9
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:16,720
 You're probably gonna interview a lot of people

10
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,820
 who can do the job, but in your opinion,

11
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,660
 what does the high performer look like?

12
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:21,940
 And then you just stop talking.

13
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,160
 You let them tell you exactly what they're looking for

14
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,780
 in the person that goes above and beyond

15
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:28,200
 to execute in this role.

16
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,660
 They will tell you the qualities of the person,

17
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,040
 they will tell you the things they do in the day-to-day,

18
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:33,000
 and they will tell you how they would like

19
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,040
 to see someone go above and beyond.

20
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:35,340
 They will literally give you

21
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:37,260
 what you're supposed to be on a silver platter,

22
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:39,940
 and your job then is to meld your skills,

23
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:41,520
 your knowledge, and your attributes

24
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,380
 to that high performer description

25
00:00:43,380 --> 00:00:44,800
 and show how you are, in fact,

26
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:46,480
 the high performer that they're looking for.

27
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:47,940
 Interviewing is just a chess game.

28
00:00:48,100 --> 00:00:50,780
 If you can get them to tell you what they're looking for,

29
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:52,580
 not to say fake your skill sets,

30
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:55,880
 but for, well, yeah, don't fake it,

31
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:58,260
 but definitely show how you are the fit

32
00:00:58,260 --> 00:00:58,900
 for the high performer.

33
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:01,020
 It isn't easy, but it is simple. Don't over complicate it.

